6. Functions of Gram Sabha.— The Gram Sabha shall perform the following functions, namely:—

(a) Consider the annual statement of accounts and the administrative report of the preceding year;
(b) Review development programmes and suggest execution policies;
(c) Identify local beneficiaries for state welfare schemes.

